  "notes": [
    "YOUR LORDSHIP (client/scenes/pages/profile_page.gd) on the painted pages' host: art/reference/profile.png, its title, portrait ring, name plate, red ribbon and three figure plates as painted (profile/page_hub).",
    "The header: the lord's round face in the ring's window (a tap opens the face picker); the name on the plate in the colour worn, with Royal Favour's seal (Look.paint_name), and the kit's quill with the rename price at the plate's end; the title worn on the ribbon, or the level; the level, might and kingdom in the crown, swords and castle plates; the crest worn -- or the one the id picks -- where the painting has its lion shield.",
    "Seven rows, the painting's seven: the row plate (profile/row) with its icon at the left, the word, and the painting's gold chevron; the mail's count in the red badge's place. FRIENDS and SETTINGS, the friends and the toggles are the painting's and are not drawn (Wave 6; the game has no sound). The rows keep the painting's order of plate and icon but take its whole frame: pitch 124 from y 512, so no hole is left under them.",
    "Every row's tap target is its plate grown to a thumb (97 tall).",
    "Stretch bands: the gaps between rows and under the last one.",
    "The three plates' figures start right of their icons' ink (crown to x 308, swords to 453, castle to 616) and end at the plates' insides (385, 540, 686). The kingdom's name takes two lines of 16 at most, no smaller than 15; a name that will not go is its tag."
